{"id": "EUVD-2026-27763", "enisaUuid": "f37911f2-7e09-33ae-95c0-89f30ff3c9e6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: qcom: q6asm: drop DSP responses for closed data streams\n\n'Commit a354f030dbce (\"ASoC: qcom: q6asm: handle the responses\nafter closing\")' attempted to ignore DSP responses arriving\nafter a stream had been closed.\n\nHowever, those responses were still handled, causing lockups.\n\nFix this by unconditionally dropping all DSP responses associated with\nclosed data streams.", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T11:28:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/414396c42ef20d2d0c9213adaf4dfa59490ca077", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c0b69245263ffa3db6f1be6e068528578fde635b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a409a64b2d61430c63cbb15d51681f13b8b0acd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3249251eac6081d5169ba09f2d9cca66ab0cab0d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a066a81ee0c1b6cdbd81393536c3b2d19ccef25"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43204", "GHSA-c79v-q7h2-4c95"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e10e903-3709-3b26-acf1-690b8237c1dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "21d20eb3-f5f9-3ceb-ad3c-08ebc2d70494", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "296fe161-8654-3a4c-a595-e2e7926e7d10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "68fd8480bb7baaf361e983f75d8571f25e017c67 <8a066a81ee0c1b6cdbd81393536c3b2d19ccef25"}, {"id": "2a4b18e4-f236-3fb2-b145-9f71f14f3921", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "2c6bbc55-629d-3b7a-8b94-8d46ab371286", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2da96c03-d7ec-3b6b-aa76-bc850b2e8dae", "product": {"name":